rthern  mexico i've been working a lot this last  year in sonora state  and that became a bit of a fiefdom for  carol quintero and he was fighting very  much their other cartel members loyal to  the sons of the drug lord el chapo it  became one of the most violent states in  mexico some very horrific gun battles so  maybe this arrest will try and reduce  that violence in sonora state as well  although there's still many players  fighting over this billions of dollars  in trafficking wealth  yeah i mean the arrest happened um  shortly after president biden met with  the president of mexico uh coincidence  uh very hard to see a complete  coincidence in this i mean right before  this visit and as i said there'd been a  slight cold relationship and there was  criticism of mexican president anders  manuel lopez obrador not really  attacking drug cartels allowing them to  operate not really going after them he  had this this famous uh phrase called  hugs not bullets referred to the drug  war  um and then anyway before this meeting  there was suddenly a bunch of very  significant busts including the biggest  bust ever the biggest seizure ever of  fentanyl now fentanyl is an opioid as a  substitute for heroin and that is really  driving a lot of the deaths the overdose  deaths in the united states last year  you saw more than 100 000  overdose deaths in the united states and  fentanyl was the biggest killer mostly  coming through mexico now this is  mind-boggling numbers if you think about  the nightmare of death happening for  this so a lot of uh pressure inside the  united states to pressure mexico to do  this and then suddenly three days after  the meeting you see the arrest of carol  quintero now this brings up the question  did the mexican government know where he  was all the time i just go and get him  or was there new information that came  from in recent days that allowed them to  make this arrest in the north of sinaloa  well it sounds like there's enough in  anot